# Served by the Workers static-asset layer for every file in dist/.
# `frame-ancestors` only works as a header, which is why the CSP is not a <meta> tag.
#
# CSP notes — verified with `pnpm preview` (wrangler dev) in a real browser:
# - script-src 'unsafe-inline' IS needed. Starlight and Expressive Code emit several
#   inline <script> blocks on every page (theme applied before first paint, code-block
#   helpers, table of contents). Their hashes change with every release, and Starlight
#   0.41 has no hook for Astro's hashed CSP (`security.csp`), so they cannot be pinned.
# - script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval' IS needed: Pagefind (Starlight's search) runs a
#   WebAssembly index; without it the search modal opens but every query fails.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline' IS needed: Expressive Code sets inline `style` attributes
#   on syntax-highlighted tokens (theme colour variables) and Starlight on the sidebar.
# Nothing else is loaded from anywhere but this origin; no fonts, no CDNs, no images.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# Hashed build output is immutable.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
